  "title": "Passage One · Healthy Eating",
  "subtitle": "青少年健康饮食干预",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "source": "2025年12月大学英语四级考试真题（第2套）· Section C · Passage One",
  "instructions": "Questions 46 to 50 are based on the following passage.",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "en": "Junk food is now a staple of many Americans’ diets. Advertising campaigns from the snack food companies, often featuring sports stars, send the message that we can neutralize any negative effects of consuming their products simply by getting more physical exercise. But recent studies show a lack of exercise is not to blame for rising obesity rates. Bad diets are.",
      "zh": "垃圾食品如今已成为许多美国人日常饮食的重要组成部分。零食公司的广告活动常由体育明星出镜，传递的信息是：只要多进行体育锻炼，就能抵消食用其产品带来的任何负面影响。但近期研究表明，肥胖率上升并非缺乏运动之过，糟糕的饮食才是原因。"
    },
    {
      "en": "Interventions (干预) to help reduce junk food consumption are especially important for children and teenagers. Prevention is better than cure because obesity is so difficult to treat. Unfortunately, while health education has shown some success among young children, teens have been harder to reach.",
      "zh": "帮助减少垃圾食品摄入的干预措施，对儿童和青少年尤为重要。预防胜于治疗，因为肥胖很难治疗。遗憾的是，尽管健康教育在低龄儿童中取得了一些成效，却更难对青少年产生影响。"
    },
    {
      "en": "Now a large-scale study has tried an innovative approach to change teenagers’ attitudes towards healthy eating, and the results are promising. The researchers argued that previous interventions have probably been unsuccessful because of a major flaw: they focused on a future, healthier you and assumed that this would be enough motivation for teenagers. In contrast, the new intervention cleverly exploits teenagers’ instinct for rebelliousness and autonomy, and the value they place on social justice.",
      "zh": "如今，一项大规模研究尝试用创新方法改变青少年对健康饮食的态度，结果令人鼓舞。研究人员认为，过去的干预可能不成功，是因为存在一个重大缺陷：它们聚焦于未来更健康的你，并假定这足以成为青少年的动力。相比之下，新干预巧妙地利用了青少年的叛逆与自主本能，以及他们对社会公正的重视。"
    },
    {
      "en": "To do this, researchers had students read an article on the food industry. It revealed a secret about the manipulative and deceptive strategies used to make junk food more addictive and characterize the products as healthy. The article also explained how advertising campaigns specifically target very young and poor people, causing harm for these vulnerable groups. Afterwards, the participants read a fictional survey of teens who wanted to “fight back against the companies by buying and eating less processed food”.",
      "zh": "为此，研究人员让学生阅读一篇关于食品行业的文章。文章揭露了一个秘密：食品行业采用操纵性和欺骗性策略，使垃圾食品更容易让人上瘾，并将这些产品描述为健康食品。文章还解释了广告活动如何专门针对低龄和贫困人群，对这些易受伤害的群体造成危害。随后，参与者阅读了一份虚构的青少年调查，其中的青少年希望“通过少买、少吃加工食品来反击这些公司”。"
    },
    {
      "en": "After the intervention, participants associated healthy eating with autonomy and social justice. The teenagers also rated healthy eating as being more appealing. Importantly, there were also some promising effects of the new intervention on actual behavior. A day later the students were offered a choice of snacks and drinks in a seemingly unrelated context. The teens chose healthy snacks and drinks (such as fruit or water) more often over unhealthy options (like biscuits and soda). Apparently associating a healthy diet with teenagers’ own values seems to be a promising avenue to prevent obesity.",
      "zh": "干预后，参与者将健康饮食与自主和社会公正联系起来。青少年也认为健康饮食更有吸引力。重要的是，新干预对实际行为也产生了一些令人鼓舞的影响。一天后，学生在一个看似无关的情境中获得了选择零食和饮料的机会。他们更多地选择水果或水等健康零食和饮料，而不是饼干和汽水等不健康的选项。显然，将健康饮食与青少年自身的价值观联系起来，似乎是一条有希望预防肥胖的途径。"
    }
  ],
